  :tender-reentry-proven
  {:title "The tender's re-entry proved under QEMU, not only on hardware"
   :needs []
   :evidence "The post-return path is exercised -- X, O and K all print -- but
              r15 is never 250 in QEMU, so :tender-step is reached once and the
              second T never appears. Seventeen re-entries were observed on
              hardware and nowhere else."
   :attempt "2026-09-09: a fixture guest was written --
             native/tender_fixture.kotoba, which counts its own entries in the
             loader-owned scratch page, prints each ordinal, and returns 250
             until the fourth. Deliberately a fixture rather than a change to
             the real guest: making production code fake a 250 to satisfy a
             test is how a gate stops meaning anything.
             It does not build, for two independent reasons, both measured.
             (1) A MINIMAL guest cannot pass verify-kotoba-native-kernel.py.
             The emitter places the RW segment at a fixed 0x108000, so a guest
             with less than about 28 KB of text leaves a gap and the checker
             refuses it for rw_start != rx_limit. Measured: rx ended 0x101950,
             rx_limit 0x102000, rw_start 0x108000. That is a latent constraint
             of the build path, not of the fixture.
             (2) WRAPPING the real kernel instead -- which would satisfy the
             size honestly and end the run the way an ordinary one does --
             fails project-link: aiueos.native.kernel is not on the fixture
             build's explicit source paths.
             Lifting either means editing a production build script for a
             test's benefit, or adding a bypass flag to a safety check.
             Neither is worth doing without the owner's word, so the file is
             kept as the concrete starting point and the node stops here."
   :blocked-on :fixture-cannot-be-built-without-changing-a-production-gate}

